      "notes": "Has two versions: one performed during blockstun or parry stun (20F start-up) and one performed as a wake-up reversal (18F start-up) · Fully invincible on frames 1-22 (blockstun) / frames 1-20 (reversal) · Armor Break (blows through all armor like Drive Impact, but not counters like JP's Amnesia) · Trying to Drive Reversal after the blockstun ends results in a Drive Impact · Drive Reversal immediately removes the current blockstun you're in and starts the attack · Causes a 4F screen freeze after the 6th start-up frame, which allows the opponent to perform a simple OS (inputting their buttons during the buffer window) to prevent their next attack from coming out · Safe on block (-2) when used against an opponent in Burnout · Costs 2 bars of Drive Gauge · If the opponent tries to throw against a wake-up Drive Reversal, it causes a 12F screen freeze and refunds 1 bar of Drive gauge (but does not prevent Burnout) · Guaranteed to interrupt any Drive Rush canceled normal if performed immediately out of blockstun (unless the opponent reacts with an invincible move or counter)",
